Track 3: The Ghost of Chronometric Junction
- Story & Context: Legend has it that at the heart of the "Chronometric Junction," where the seven ancient bus routes once converged, the Grid-Haunters achieved apotheosis, their collective digital disruption creating a time-dilation effect that allowed a phantom streetcar, laden with the souls of forgotten commuters, to appear for exactly one spectral minute before dissolving back into static, and a strange, crystalline digital hum resonated long after, marking the place as forever sacred to their anti-system faith: "Hear the engines hum, broken but never truly gone."
